Enhancement: Refuse to sign a repository checkout in the release workflow

The release workflow now builds ocsign from v0.3.0, which exits 1 when the tree
being signed holds a `.git` entry at any depth. Signing a working copy instead of
the packaged app payload produces a technically valid signature that covers
tests, CI config and version-control internals as part of the app, and nothing
downstream can tell it apart from a correct one. The workflow already points
ocsign at the appstore staging directory, so this is a backstop that fires only
if an app's Makefile aims signing at the checkout root.

https://github.com/owncloud/reusable-workflows/pull/93
